    objectId:'81630',objectUse:'The Worth ball gown’s silk, glass, and metallic thread evidence extraordinary skilled transformation while the catalog record does not name the individual hands. The gap is itself evidence—never permission to invent them.',
    outputs:['Canonical essay: Beyond the Romance of the Hand','Ten-minute labor-and-value film','Nine-frame credit-is-not-compensation carousel','Five craft-power verticals','Craft Obligation Ledger','Newsletter, procurement, classroom, and worker-review editions'],
    platform:['LONG VIDEO — Begin at the glittering surface, then trace each verified material and task backward toward price, time, safety, pay, voice, and remedy. Leave unknown workers visibly unnamed rather than fabricating completeness.','SHORT 01 — “Credit is not compensation.” Add: compensation is not safety; visibility is not bargaining power; heritage is not consent.','SHORT 02 — The purchase-order test: did price, lead time, revisions, and cancellation terms make lawful and safe work possible?','CAROUSEL — Nine obligations: identify; consent; contract; pay; time; safety; voice; remedy; preserve. Each frame includes a verification field.','AUDIO — A worker-review protocol with interpreter, anonymity, stopping, correction, and publication-consent choices.','PROCUREMENT — A pre-order worksheet that routes jurisdiction-specific wage, classification, safety, and contracting questions to qualified local review.']
