    platform:['LONG VIDEO — Open with a creator already carrying clients, collaborators, files, accounts, invoices, and promises. Build the practice map, then draw a bright line before entity, tax, liability, and employment claims.','SHORT 01 — “You can have an institution before you have a company. You cannot have an LLC merely because you operate like one.”','SHORT 02 — Seven things to organize before the adviser meeting: parties, promises, money, rights, accounts, records, risks.','CAROUSEL — PRACTICE / PROMISE / PEOPLE / MONEY / RIGHTS / RECORDS / RISK / STRUCTURE / TRANSITION / PROFESSIONAL REVIEW.','NEWSLETTER — Subject: The house may exist before the company. Explain the two thresholds and provide the adviser-ready transition inventory.','ADVISER PREP — A neutral fact pack: activity, jurisdictions, parties, revenue, expenses, workers, facilities, contracts, IP records, data, insurance, liabilities, goals, and unanswered questions.']
