    platform:['LONG VIDEO — Follow one look backward from runway image to research, pattern, sample, fitting, sourcing, production, styling, image, press, sales, and archive. Put VERIFIED, INFERENCE, PROPOSAL, and UNRESOLVED on screen; never invent a role because the industry usually has one.','SHORT 01 — “The designer is the headline. The collection is an institution.” Reveal one handoff at a time, ending with the missing fields: pay, approval, credit, ownership, remedy.','SHORT 02 — “A credit list is not a power map.” Split preferred public credit from contract role, decision authority, compensation, and correction rights.','CAROUSEL — ONE LOOK / WHO RESEARCHED? / WHO PATTERNED? / WHO SAMPLED? / WHO FIT? / WHO MADE? / WHO STYLED? / WHO IMAGED? / WHO APPROVED? / WHO WAS PAID? / WHO OWNS WHAT? / WHO CAN CORRECT?','NEWSLETTER — Subject: The institution hiding behind one collection. Give readers the constellation worksheet and explain why actual records—not romantic assumptions—must populate it.','CONTRIBUTOR REVIEW — A private pre-publication sheet for every named person to verify spelling, role, scope, confidentiality, preferred credit, and unresolved dispute without forcing agreement on ownership.']
